export default {"X000100":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A finite étale cyclotomic algebra with unit Vandermonde differences</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000231\"><span>Étale ring map</span><code>P000231</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000203\"><span>Finite ring map</span><code>P000203</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000100\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000100</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000211\"><span>Surjective ring map</span><code>P000211</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Ring homomorphisms</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Take <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">𝐙</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R=\\mathbf Z[1/p]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> for a prime <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p\\ge3</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> and <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Φ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S=R[X]/(\\Phi_p)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. The monic degree <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">p-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> presentation makes <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> free of rank at least two, so <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R\\to S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> is not surjective. In <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the factorization of <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T^p-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> into linear terms has unit derivative at every root, so the differences between distinct roots are units. The monic presentation therefore also has invertible derivative, giving a finite étale <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>-algebra.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03GF\">Stacks 03GF · numbered source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-03GF\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000100\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000100\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000101":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A completion at an infinitely generated maximal ideal that fails completeness</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000080\"><span>Local ring</span><code>P000080</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000101\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000101</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000122\"><span>Complete local ring</span><code>P000122</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Commutative rings</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Localize <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">k[X_1,X_2,\\ldots]</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> at the ideal generated by all variables, and take its completion there. The resulting ring is local. Its maximal ideal strictly contains the extension of the original maximal ideal, and the ring fails completeness for its own maximal ideal, as shown by the completion calculation in Stacks 05JC.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JC\">Stacks 05JC · numbered source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/examples/#tag-05JC\">Index</a> · <a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0324\">Stacks 0324 · numbered source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/algebra/#tag-0324\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000101\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000101\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>","X000102":"<article class=\"algebra-card\" data-algebra-kind=\"example\" data-relation-style=\"example\"><header><span class=\"algebra-type\">Counterexample or example</span><h3>A finitely presented quotient with non-quasi-compact smooth locus</h3></header><div class=\"algebra-sequent\"><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Holds in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000211\"><span>Surjective ring map</span><code>P000211</code></a><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000202\"><span>Ring map of finite presentation</span><code>P000202</code></a></div><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">─</span><a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000102\" class=\"algebra-relation-code\" title=\"Open shared record\">X000102</a><span class=\"algebra-stroke\" aria-hidden=\"true\">∥</span><div class=\"algebra-lane\"><span class=\"algebra-lane-title\">Fails in this example</span><a class=\"algebra-node\" href=\"#P000746\"><span>Quasi-compact smooth locus of a ring map</span><code>P000746</code></a></div></div><p class=\"property-context\">Domain: Ring homomorphisms</p><p><strong>Witness.</strong> Take <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R=k[x,y_1,y_2,\\ldots]/(xy_i:i\\ge1)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> over a field and <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A=R/(x)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. The map is an isomorphism on each <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(y_i)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>. At the remaining point, the origin in <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Spec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Spec}(A)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>, the nonzero ideal generated by <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> prevents flatness of the local quotient. The opens <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D(y_i)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> cover the smooth locus and no finite subfamily suffices, as may be seen by setting all but one <span class=\"atlas-math\"><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y_i</annotation></semantics></math></span></span> equal to zero.</p><p class=\"property-references\"><a href=\"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07CB\">Stacks 07CB · Numbered Stacks Project source</a> <a class=\"algebra-index-ref\" href=\"../topologies/database/stacks/smoothing/#tag-07CB\">Index</a></p><p class=\"algebra-links\"><a href=\"#X000102\">Permalink</a> · <a href=\"../topologies/database/#X000102\">Shared catalogue</a></p></article>"};
